  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Plain-English Summary:</strong> HowdyNET collects only the information needed to provide our services and respond to inquiries. We do not sell your personal data. We use it to keep you informed, serve you better, and comply with legal obligations.
  </div>

  <!-- 1 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="who-we-are">
    <span class="section-num">Section 01</span>
    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>HowdyNET ("we," "us," or "our") is a managed technology services provider headquartered in Austin, Texas. We provide internet connectivity, local area network (LAN) solutions, managed IT services, and related technology support to businesses and individuals primarily throughout Texas and the United States.</p>
    <p>This Privacy Policy describes how we handle personal information collected through our website (<strong>howdynet.io</strong>), our network quality test tools, our contact and quote forms, and any other services we offer online or offline.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="data-collected">
    <span class="section-num">Section 02</span>
    <h2>Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect the following categories of personal information:</p>

    <p><strong>Information You Provide Directly</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name and job title</li>
      <li>Business name and address</li>
      <li>Email address and phone number</li>
      <li>Message content from contact, quote, and support forms</li>
      <li>Mailing list subscription preferences</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Technical & Usage Data (Collected Automatically)</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>IP address and general geolocation (city/state level)</li>
      <li>Browser type, operating system, and device type</li>
      <li>Pages visited, time on page, and referring URL</li>
      <li>Network quality test results (latency, jitter, packet loss, bufferbloat score) — associated with your session, not permanently linked to your identity unless you submit a form</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>We do NOT collect:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Social Security Numbers, government ID numbers</li>
      <li>Payment card numbers or bank account information (we use third-party processors for any billing)</li>
      <li>Sensitive personal data categories (health data, racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, etc.)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="how-we-collect">
    <span class="section-num">Section 03</span>
    <h2>How We Collect Your Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Forms:</strong> Contact, quote request, network test results, and mailing list signup forms on our website.</li>
      <li><strong>Automated tools:</strong> Cookies, server logs, and analytics platforms (see Section 8 — Cookies).</li>
      <li><strong>Network diagnostics:</strong> Our browser-based network quality test runs entirely client-side. Raw test data is not transmitted to our servers unless you choose to submit it via a form.</li>
      <li><strong>Direct communication:</strong> Emails, phone calls, or in-person meetings you initiate with us.</li>
      <li><strong>Third-party referrals:</strong> Publicly available business directories or referrals from existing clients.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="how-we-use">
    <span class="section-num">Section 04</span>
    <h2>How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <p>We use collected information for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Responding to inquiries, quotes, and support requests</li>
      <li>Delivering contracted services and managing client accounts</li>
      <li>Sending newsletters, service updates, or promotional content (only if you have opted in)</li>
      <li>Improving our website, tools, and services through analytics</li>
      <li>Complying with legal obligations and resolving disputes</li>
      <li>Fraud detection and network security</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="callout callout-orange">
      <strong>No spam, ever.</strong> We will only send you marketing communications if you explicitly subscribe. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in any email we send.
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="sharing">
    <span class="section-num">Section 05</span>
    <h2>Sharing & Disclosure</h2>
    <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We may share your data only in the following limited circumstances:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> Vendors who help us operate (e.g., web hosting and edge security via Cloudflare, email delivery, CRM software). Our browser-based network test also queries a third-party IP geolocation service (ipapi.co) to display your approximate location and ISP; that request carries your IP address and is subject to that provider's privacy policy. These vendors are contractually bound to protect your data and may not use it for their own purposes.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> When required by law, court order, or governmental authority.</li>
      <li><strong>Business transfers:</strong> In the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, your information may transfer to the successor entity, with notice provided to you.</li>
      <li><strong>With your consent:</strong> For any other purpose, only if you expressly authorize it.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="retention">
    <span class="section-num">Section 06</span>
    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain personal data for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes described in this policy, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. In general:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Contact form submissions: up to 3 years</li>
      <li>Client service records: up to 7 years (for tax and compliance purposes)</li>
      <li>Newsletter subscriber records: until you unsubscribe, plus 90 days</li>
      <li>Web server logs: up to 12 months</li>
    </ul>
    <p>After these periods, data is securely deleted or anonymized.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="your-rights">
    <span class="section-num">Section 07</span>
    <h2>Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location, you may have the following rights with respect to your personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access:</strong> Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction:</strong> Request that we correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> Request that we delete your personal data ("right to be forgotten"), subject to legal retention requirements.</li>
      <li><strong>Opt-out of marketing:</strong> Unsubscribe from marketing communications at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Data portability:</strong> Request your data in a portable format.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction or objection:</strong> Object to certain types of processing.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Texas Residents:</strong> The Texas Data Privacy and Security Act (TDPSA) grants additional rights including the right to opt out of the sale of personal data (we don't sell data) and the right to appeal a denied request. Contact us at the address below to exercise any of these rights.
    </div>
    <p>We will respond to verified requests within 30 days. We may need to verify your identity before processing a request.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 8 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="cookies">
    <span class="section-num">Section 08</span>
    <h2>Cookies & Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>We use cookies and similar technologies to operate our website and understand how visitors use it. The types of cookies we use:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies:</strong> Required for core site functionality (e.g., form submission, spam protection via Cloudflare Turnstile, remembering your cookie choice). Cannot be disabled.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> Help us understand traffic patterns (e.g., page views, time on site). These may be provided by third-party analytics services. You can opt out via your browser settings or a cookie consent banner.</li>
      <li><strong>Preference cookies:</strong> Remember your settings or choices.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings. Disabling analytics cookies will not affect core site functionality. We do not use cookies to serve targeted advertising.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 9 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="security">
    <span class="section-num">Section 09</span>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>We take the security of your data seriously. Our measures include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>HTTPS encryption for all data transmitted to and from our website</li>
      <li>Access controls limiting who can view personal data internally</li>
      <li>Secure, reputable hosting infrastructure (Cloudflare)</li>
      <li>Regular review of data handling practices</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure. In the event of a data breach that affects your personal information, we will notify affected individuals as required by applicable law.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 10 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="children">
    <span class="section-num">Section 10</span>
    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>Our services are directed to businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under the age of 13. If you believe we have inadvertently collected data from a child, please contact us and we will promptly delete it.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 11 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="changes">
    <span class="section-num">Section 11</span>
    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will update the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page. If we make material changes, we will notify you via email (if you are subscribed) or a notice on our website. Your continued use of our services after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 12 -->
  <section class="policy-section" id="contact-us">
    <span class="section-num">Section 12</span>
    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>To exercise your rights, ask questions about this policy, or report a privacy concern, please reach out to us:</p>
  </section>

  <div class="contact-card">
    <h3>HowdyNET Privacy Contact</h3>
    <p><strong style="color:#fff;">HowdyNET</strong></p>
    <p>Austin, Texas, United States</p>
    <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@howdynet.io">support@howdynet.io</a></p>
    <p>Website: <a href="https://www.howdynet.io">howdynet.io</a></p>
    <p style="margin-top:1rem; font-size:0.82rem; color:rgba(255,255,255,0.4);">We aim to respond to all privacy requests within 5 business days.</p>
  </div>
</Legal>
